COPY public.bankresume (subject, topic, question, answer, expected_concepts, difficulty, question_hash) FROM stdin;
Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)	encapsulation	In Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), What is encapsulation, and what problem does it address in a production service?	Encapsulation keeps an object's state behind a controlled interface so callers depend on operations rather than representation. In Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), its boundary separates the decision about encapsulation from unrelated implementation details in a production service. The definition perspective is correct only when encapsulation preserves predictable results as a production service changes load, input, or concurrency. For example, begin with a small encapsulation case, inspect its invariant, and then repeat the check with a representative a production service workload. One limitation is that encapsulation can add resource or coordination cost when the workload grows. For Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), the decision is justified when the measured behavior of encapsulation matches the stated requirement.	encapsulation, Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), definition, correctness, trade-offs	Easy	6e365c24525f3b3aa325fc07f88c1233148d3742b78da14cf917f47c543d66cb
Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)	encapsulation	In Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), What is encapsulation, and what problem does it address in a command-line utility?	Encapsulation keeps an object's state behind a controlled interface so callers depend on operations rather than representation. In Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), its boundary separates the decision about encapsulation from unrelated implementation details in a command-line utility. The definition perspective is correct only when encapsulation preserves predictable results as a command-line utility changes load, input, or concurrency. For example, begin with a small encapsulation case, inspect its invariant, and then repeat the check with a representative a command-line utility workload. Its boundary is important because encapsulation cannot compensate for an incorrect contract elsewhere in the design. For Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), the decision is justified when the measured behavior of encapsulation matches the stated requirement.	encapsulation, Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), definition, correctness, trade-offs	Easy	f3d9b03389c9d93c257d5328b9e4f6283b0c9d0ecbaa3baf5dbdd53dd1c399b0
